     DIGITAL MOVES TO LEAD HIGH-SPEED PCI NETWORK ADAPTER MARKET


            ...Offers top price/performance for customers
                      seeking easy migration...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 27, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today moved to take the lead in the emerging market for high-speed 
PCI (Peripheral Component Interconnect) network adapters by 
introducing an aggressively priced scalable Fast Ethernet PCI 
adapter.  Operating at either 10 or 100 Mb/s, the Fast EtherWORKS 
PCI 10/100 adapter provides a simple, cost-effective migration path 
from the 10 Mb/s networks most customers have today to faster 100 
Mb/s networks.  Also, the Company solidified its lead in the 10 Mb/s 
portion of the PCI market by reducing prices up to 28% on its 
current offerings and releasing compelling test results. 

     "Digital intends to be the market share leader in PCI network
adapters," said Bill Maro, vice president of product marketing and
engineering for Digital's Network Product Business.  "We offer PCI
adapters with excellent price/performance across a number of
technologies, helping customers leverage their existing networks to
compete more effectively."  Digital currently offers Ethernet, Fast
Ethernet, and FDDI adapters. 

     "Digital is set to be a major player in the PCI adapter 
market," said Michael Howard, president of Infonetics Research, a 
network industry research and consulting firm. "The new PCI Fast 
Ethernet adapter is very fast and competitively priced." 

Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 Adapter 

     The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 adapter is designed to offer 
high data throughput with low CPU utilization.  Key for compute-
intensive applications, this design also provides potential cost 
savings by allowing more client connections per server.  The adapter 
operates at 10 or 100 Mb/s, automatically sensing the correct 
operating speed.  It operates at up to 200 Mb/s in full duplex mode.

     The new adapter, like all of Digital's PCI adapters, is 
supported by major network operating systems, including NetWare, 
Windows, and UNIX systems.  The adapter offers "plug-and-play" 
installation and a lifetime warranty. 

     The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 adapter is priced at $249 and 
will ship in the second quarter of calendar year 1995.

EtherWORKS Turbo PCI Adapters Lead Market in Price and Performance

     Digital has taken the price/performance lead in the 10 Mb/s 
Ethernet PCI adapter market by cutting the prices of its EtherWORKS 
Turbo PCI adapters by up to 28%.  The EtherWORKS Turbo PCI Combo, 
which includes twisted-pair, AUI, and ThinWire connections, now 
lists for $179.  The twisted-pair-only version, the EtherWORKS Turbo 
PCI TP, is now $149.

     The Company also reported NetBench 3.0 performance results 
showing that the EtherWORKS Turbo PCI adapters have better CPU 
utilization than competitive products shipping today.  In one 
instance, this meant that a server using an EtherWORKS Turbo PCI 
adapter served more than twice the number of client stations than 
the same server using a competitor's adapter.

Customer Cites Excellent Performance and Price

     "We've found the PCI adapters to be excellent performers," said 
Wayne Church, network manager for ITT Hartford Insurance Group's 
Personal Lines Insurance Center, a division that sells directly to 
older Americans.  "The price is very attractive as well -- 
especially since we buy direct and have the adapter bundled with the 
PC."  The division uses EtherWORKS PCI Turbo PCI adapters in PCs 
running Windows and a terminal emulation package to run a mainframe 
insurance policy-writing application.  The Ethernet adapters connect 
Digital PCs to a mainframe gateway, which in turn connects to the 
mainframe.

     Building on a strong tradition of technological excellence, 
Digital is leading the way in the networking industry today.  
According to revenue figures from the International Data Corporation 
(IDC), Dataquest, and Rising Star Research, Digital holds the number 
three market position in routers, hubs and LAN switching markets, 
and holds the number two position in FDDI technology. Digital's 
Network Product Business has pioneered a new, converged model for 
networking in which hubs, routers and switches are deployed on an 
integrated platform.  In addition, Digital's expertise in network 
integration services has connected more than 13 million users 
worldwide. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software, and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
