                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100


OVERVIEW:

The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 is a high performance Ethernet
adapter that allows users of PCI bus architecture systems to connect
to 10 Mb/s or 100 Mb/s Ethernet networks. It also provides a cost-
effective migration path for existing Ethernet users planning to 
upgrade to Fast Ethernet. Link speed selection is automatic. 

The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 is designed to offer high data
throughput with low CPU utilization. Important when using compute-
intensive applications, this feature also provides potential cost 
savings by allowing more client connections per server.  All major 
network operating systems are supported. 


KEY FEATURES/BENEFITS:

High performance parallel        Maximizes data throughput while
cut-through bus-master           minimizing CPU utilization and
architecture                     thereby provides fast network file 
                                 transfers, etc., at either Ethernet 
                                 or Fast Ethernet speeds. Also 
                                 increases potential client/server 
                                 ratio, reducing system investment. 

Automatic link speed		 Adapter automatically adjusts to 10
selection                        or 100 Mb/s network speeds, 
                                 eliminating the need to service the 
                                 desktop or server connections as 
                                 Fast Ethernet repeaters or switches 
                                 are added to the network.

Full duplex capable              Provides up to twice normal network
     				 bandwidth (20 Mb/s or 200 Mb/s) 
                                 when connected to full duplex 
                                 capable switches or used in point-
     				 to-point connections. Useful for 
                                 demanding high bandwidth 
                                 applications such as video, file 
                                 transfer and system back-up 
                                 operations.

Ease of use and operation        A unique install/configuration 
                                 utility makes installation easy. In 
                                 addition, the adapter has automatic 
                                 speed selection and full adherence 
                                 to the plug-and-play features of 
                                 the PCI bus. LEDs are provided for 
                                 visual diagnostics. All major 
                                 network operating systems are 
                                 supported. Driver software upgrades 
                                 are widely available on-line, e.g., 
                                 CompuServe and the Internet.

Lifetime warranty                The adapter carries a lifetime 
                                 warranty (subject to the terms and 
                                 conditions of the warranty 
                                 registration card). Adapter 
                                 investments are thereby protected.

Service and support              The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 is
                                 backed by Digital Equipment 
                                 Corporation's worldwide service and
                                 support organization.


HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS:

The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 can currently be used in Intel, 
Alpha, POWERPC and MIPS platforms that are compliant with the PCI 
Local Bus V2.0 specification and support PCI BIOS V2.0. The adapter 
supports a 5 volt PCI bus master slot. 

A single RJ45 connector is provided for attachment to unshielded
twisted pair wiring. TIA/EIA 568A Category 3, 4 & 5 twisted pair
wiring is acceptable for 10BaseT operation, however, TIA/EIA 568A
Category 5 twisted pair wiring must be used to support 100BASE-TX
operation, in accordance with the IEEE 802.3 100BASE-TX 
specification.


SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS:

The following software drivers are shipped with each adapter for use
in Intel platforms: NetWare DOS ODI client, NetWare 3.x ODI server,
NetWare 4.x ODI server, DOS client, Windows 3.1, Windows for
Workgroups 3.11, OS/2 and SCO UNIX. 

Windows NT support for all platforms is distributed with the 
operating system and supported directly by Microsoft. 

OpenVMS and OSF/1 support is currently available on Alpha platforms.
Support on individual Alpha platforms will be announced 
independently.


PRICING/AVAILABILITY:

The Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 (DE500-XA) is priced at $249 each.
Volume shipments will commence in Q2, calendar year 1995. 
