                       DIGITAL NAMES GWYN PUGH
     VICE PRESIDENT OF MANUFACTURING AND DISTRIBUTION -- EUROPE
                    FOR THE SYSTEMS BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the appointment of Gwyn Pugh as vice president of 
Manufacturing and Distribution -- Europe for the Systems Business 
Unit (SBU).

     In this position, Pugh, 46, will be responsible for 
competitively sourcing, manufacturing, supplying and delivering SBU 
hardware and software products to Digital's customers in Europe and 
Digital's partners worldwide. He will report to Charles P. Goslee, 
vice president of Worldwide Manufacturing and Distribution for the 
Systems Business Unit.

     Prior to joining Digital, Pugh was a general manager and Board 
member of Motorola UK Limited. In that position, he was responsible 
for the initial start-up and very successful growth of Motorola's 
cellular telephone manufacturing facility in Bathgate, Scotland. 
Opened in 1990, as a green field site, that facility now employs 
more than 2,000 people and has an annual turnover of $2B. Before 
joining Motorola, he held senior engineering and production 
management positions with Philips Electronics Components and Pye 
Ltd.  

     Pugh holds a higher national diploma in Production Engineering 
and is a member of the British Institute of Management.

     "We are extremely pleased to have someone with Gwyn's 
distinguished track record in cost, quality and high-volume 
manufacturing," said Charles P. Goslee.  "With his credentials, 
Gwyn is the person we want to lead our European Manufacturing and 
Distribution organization in its drive to increased levels of 
customer satisfaction."

