        DIGITAL'S HIGH PERFORMANCE ALL-PENTIUM LINE FEATURES
                   SINGLE- AND DUAL-PROCESSOR PCs


          ...Workstation-class Performance at PC prices...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 6, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
boosted its award-winning XL technology today with the introduction 
of its new Celebris XL line of Pentium processor-based PCs, 
replacing the popular DECpc XL series.  The Celebris XL systems 
offer PC power users workstation-class performance and maximum 
investment protection at PC prices.  The seven new deskside models 
-- three fully configured and four configured specifically for 
resellers -- include powerful features, such as:

      o	 choice of 90MHz and 100MHz single- and dual-processor 
         Pentium systems;
      o	 64-bit graphics accelerators, PCI/ISA subsystems and burst 
         cache for increased performance;
      o	 upgrades to dual-Pentium and Alpha processors for maximum 
         investment protection;
      o	 ease-of-use features for advanced productivity; and
      o	 wide operating system support for application flexibility

     The Celebris XL line is the sixth in the series of major new 
product introductions from Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit 
over the past six months.  The Celebris XL family completes the move 
to Digital's new naming convention and includes its acclaimed 
"Getting Started" software that helps users become productive, more 
quickly.

     "The Celebris XL line builds on the popular DECpc XL features 
that gained wide customer acceptance," said Bernhard Auer, vice 
president and general manager of Digital's PC Business Unit.  
"Today's new processors and features, combined with the new ease-
of-use features, give us the "hottest" desktop for PC power users 
on the market today."

High Performance PCs

     The Celebris XL line includes five models: two single- and one 
dual-processor 90MHz systems; and both single- and dual-processor 
100MHz systems to help meet the complex computing needs of business 
and scientific users.  The new systems feature S3 Vision864 and 
Diamond Stealth 64-bit PCI video accelerator controllers, and 
leading-edge PCI/ISA I/O subsystems.  Three of the models feature 
synchronous burst cache memory, which increases performance by up 
to 10 percent over systems with standard cache memory.  Celebris XL 
benchmarks include a Winstone '95 benchmark rating of 145.9 and a 
DOS Mark 16 rating of 963.63. 

     The no-compromise performance of the Celebris XL line is 
well-suited for PC users who run multiple applications and databases 
as well as applications in graphical design and CAD, software 
development, statistical analysis, and desktop publishing.   

Maximum Investment Protection: Upgradeable to Dual Pentium and Alpha

     Using an innovative motherboard/daughtercard modular design, 
the Celebris XL line provides an unparalleled upgrade path from 
Pentium single-processor to Pentium dual-processor to Alpha 
processors.  Called the PowerGrade program, the upgrade capability 
offers superior investment protection and is ideal for buyers who 
need a top-of-the-line CISC platform today, but may require RISC 
architecture in the future.

     "The Celebris XL family gives customers no-compromise 
performance, award-winning architecture and leading-edge 
functionality," said Howard Elias, vice president, Desktop Product 
Line.  "And because the Celebris XL line is processor independent, 
it is one of the most expandable and upgradeable PCs in the world."

Product Functionality: Easy to Use, Easy to Install, Easy to Deploy

     The state-of-the-art functionality of Digital's Celebris XL 
line makes it easy to use from the time users power-on the system.  
The new systems implement dynamic Plug and Play technology, which 
allows users to automatically configure add-in cards.  Advanced 
Power Management (APM) features include system/suspend time-outs, 
hard disk drive time-outs, and a quick hot key.  APM reduces system 
power consumption, resulting in lower operating costs.

     The Celebris XL line is easy to install and easy to deploy.  
The products come in easy-to-open packaging and include a fold-out 
"Quick Set-up Users Guide."  The systems feature Digital's "Getting 
Started" enhanced user interface software for easy system set-up at 
power on.  In addition, the Celebris XL systems are the first 
Digital PCs to provide on-line documentation for MS-DOS and Windows 
for Workgroups.  The easy-to-access screwless deskside enclosure 
offers maximum expansion but is compact enough to sit on top of, or 
beside, a desk. 

     Digital's Celebris XL line is Desktop Management Interface 
(DMI) ready, which will provide significant advancements in network 
administration of an organization's client/server computing 
environment.  DMI will allow desktop client hardware and software 
status reporting, asset management across a network, remote 
diagnostics of client PCs, and improved management of a company's 
enterprise-wide, distributed computing environment.

High Performance Operating System Support and Value Added Software

     The Celebris XL line comes installed with MS-DOS and Microsoft 
Windows for Workgroups and a variety of value-added software, such 
as QA Plus diagnostic software for users and systems administrators 
and a diskette back-up utility for pre-installed software.  The 
systems are also Microsoft Windows 95 ready.  In addition, the 
Celebris XL line supports a wide selection of certified network 
operating systems, including Windows NT, Banyan Vines, Novell 
NetWare and Digital PATHWORKS.  NeXTstep, OS/2, OS/2 SMP and SCO 
UNIX will be certified in the future.

Pricing and Availability

     Prices range from an entry-level Celebris XL 590 single-
processor system priced at $2,649 to a dual-processor Celebris XL 
5100 at $4,799.  Four Celebris XL systems are configured as single- 
and dual-processor 90MHz and 100MHz models and do not include hard 
drives.  The new PC line also comes with Digital's worldwide service 
and support through a limited three-year warranty, including 
one-year on-site, where available.  

     The Celebris XL 590 models and the Alpha PowerGrade upgrade are 
available immediately.  The Celebris XL 5100 models and the dual 
Pentium PowerGrade upgrade will be available later this quarter.

     The systems are available through Digital's channel partners, 
including resellers, distributors, and dealers as well as through 
Digital's direct sales organization.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
