                      DIGITAL NAMES SULTAN ZIA
                        VICE PRESIDENT OF ITS
           VIDEO INTERACTIVE INFORMATION SERVICES BUSINESS


           ...Appointment underscores Digital's commitment
                     to video server market ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 7, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the appointment of Sultan Zia as vice president of 
its Video Interactive Information Services (VIIS) business, 
reporting to William Strecker, vice president of the Advanced 
Technology Group and Chief Technical Officer.  The appointment is 
effective immediately.

     Zia, 53, has managed VIIS as an integrated startup business for 
Digital since its inception last year.  VIIS is chartered with 
developing solutions that make it possible to deliver cost-effective 
interactive programming to mass markets.  Under Zia's management, 
VIIS has led the industry with powerful media server technology and 
strategic alliances that enable end-to-end interactive solutions.  
VIIS, which is one of three key businesses that comprise Digital's 
Advanced Technology Group, is at the forefront of this emerging 
market.

     "Interactive video is poised for explosive growth," stated 
Strecker.  "As the leading vendor in delivering large scale 
interactive video information systems, we are uniquely positioned to 
capitalize on this burgeoning market and the future revenue growth 
it promises."

     While other companies have been pre-announcing offerings and 
long-term plans, Digital has already delivered solutions for a range 
of trials and deployments, and has opened the first of several 
Digital Media Studios that will provide consumers with an array of 
interactive information programs.  In the past twelve months, under 
Zia's leadership, Digital has achieved significant milestones, 
making the company a leader in global interactive information 
services:

     o 	Industry's most deployments/trials -- Digital's media server 
        has been selected by more telecommunications and cable 
        companies worldwide than any other vendor, including US 
        West's trial already underway in Nebraska; NYNEX deployments 
        in Rhode Island, Massachusetts, and Maine; Svenska Kabel-
     	TV's trial in Sweden; Telstra/Telecom's first pilot program 
        in Australia; and, most recently, Ameritech has chosen 
        Digital to provide the media server platform for Ameritech's 
        interactive services deployment in communities in the 
        Midwestern Unites States.

     o 	Leading vendor alliances -- VIIS has formed alliances with 
        the leading set-top box, networking, switching, software and 
        content providers, to ensure seamless integration of all 
        components in the end-to-end solution.  Digital's publicly 
        announced alliances include Broadband Technologies, 
        Compression Labs, MicroMall, and Microware Systems, as well 
        as leading set-top box vendors:  Apple Computer, Compression
       	Labs, General Instrument, Goldstar, Mitsubishi, Philips 
        Consumer Electronics, Samsung, Scientific Atlanta, Stellar 
        One Corporation, and Zenith.

     o 	Industry's only complete content creation center targeting 
        multiple networks -- the company opened its first Digital 
        Media Studio, in Tarrytown, N.Y., providing complete content 
        creation resources.  Digital is planning additional Digital 
        Media Studios in strategic locations worldwide to assist the 
        wide range of content providers globally.

     o 	Shaping industry standards -- Digital actively participates 
        in several standards-setting bodies designed to create a 
        common architecture to facilitate the delivery of 
        interactive information services, including: Digital Audio 
        Video Interoperability Committee (DAVIC); ISO/MPEG on the 
        DSM-CC set-top box interface standard; and the Interactive 
        Multimedia Association (IMA).

     A 22-year Digital veteran, Zia spearheaded the company's effort 
in high-end VAX systems and spent several years as technology 
manager for the company's Networks and Communications business.

     He earned a bachelor's degree in India, a master's degree in 
electrical engineering from Kansas State University, and is a 
graduate of the Advanced International Management Program at INSEAD 
in Fountainbleau, France.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
