               WATERS CORPORATION SELECTS DIGITAL PCs
          TO SELL WITH ITS CHROMATOGRAPHY SOFTWARE PRODUCTS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 13, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Waters Corporation has chosen Digital personal 
computers as its primary microcomputer platform for its Millennium 
family of products. For the first time, Waters is packaging its 
chromatography software with PCs and providing worldwide support 
from both Waters and Digital. Waters has sold its software for 
Digital VAX computers since 1987. 

     Companies in areas such as pharmaceutical, chemical, 
petrochemical, and food and beverage industries rely on Waters' 
analytical instrumentation for manufacturing and quality control 
operations.

     Millennium software can be used in standalone PCs or networked, 
client/server environments providing the flexibility needed to meet 
customer requirements.  Millennium features a Windows-based 
interface to data stored on an Oracle database server.  Digital 
Venturis 486-based PCs and Digital Celebris Pentium class systems 
are available with the Millennium 2010 Chromatography Manager.  
Servers include Digital Prioris XL 590, VAX/OpenVMS, and 
Alpha/OpenVMS systems for the Millennium 2020 Client/Server 
Networks. 

     Greg Murphy, director, worldwide data products at Waters 
Corporation said: "Digital's experience with OEM manufacturers and 
its ability to maintain product consistency from one revision to the 
next are important.  Our customers are able to maintain a state of 
validation wherever it is needed, which is critical to the 
chromatography Industry."

     In addition to the range of Digital hardware options, users of 
Millenium software will benefit from Digital's PATHWORKS networking 
software.  It ties together PCs and servers into an enterprise-wide 
system for the rapid distribution of data and the timely analysis of 
that data.  "With the addition of Digital PCs, Millennium customers 
can now take advantage of the breadth and depth of computers, 
software, and support offered by this partnership with Waters," 
explains Tony Amico, director, channels marketing, Digital's 
Personal Computer Business Unit.  

     Murphy adds, "Industry regulations make it imperative that data 
be available at anytime and that's why prompt field service wherever 
it is needed is included as a critical part of this relationship.  
Digital has an established reputation for worldwide support."

     Waters is the industry leader in the $1.4 billion worldwide 
industry for high performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) 
analytical instruments and columns.  The Company produces a range of 
instruments, information management systems, and chromatography 
chemistry products for HPLC and related applications.  

     The Company was founded in 1958.  Worldwide headquarters is in 
Milford, Massachusetts.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
