MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 13, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced price reductions of up to 19 percent on four Digital 
HiNote color notebook models in the United States, Latin America, 
and the Caribbean.  The list price reductions range from $200 U.S. 
to $770 U.S. on four of the five HiNote models.

     The HiNote family, designed and engineered by Digital, sets a 
new standard for notebook computing.  The HiNote family offers full 
functionality, combined with industry leading design, ergonomics, 
and aesthetics in a light and thin form factor.  The breakthrough 
design of the HiNote family -- including a 9.5 inch full color 
screen, full-size keyboards, sculptured palm rest, and a unique 
ambidextrous trackball, to name only a few -- come in a 1.5 inch 
high, 5.5 pound package.  When introduced last fall at COMDEX, BIS 
Strategic Decisions reported that "the HiNote notebooks were the hit 
of the show based on the crowds in the Digital booth...Digital has 
entered the mobile market with a vengeance, rising from obscurity to 
star status overnight."    

