                   DIGITAL ADDS NEW PENTIUM MODELS
                    TO ITS STARION PC RETAIL LINE


    ...First PC Vendor to Offer Entirely Pentium Processor-Based
         Retail PC Product Line with Three-Year Warranty...


      ...Signs Incredible Universe and Nobody Beats the Wiz...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 14, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it is the first PC vendor to offer an entire 
Pentium processor-based PC line, with a three-year limited warranty, 
in the retail market.  This latest offering reinforces Digital's 
commitment to deliver the latest technology complemented by premiere 
service and support.  With the introduction of eight new 75MHz, 
90MHz and 100MHz models in its popular Starion line, the company 
also announced it has signed agreements with Incredible Universe and 
Nobody Beats the Wiz, consumer electronics superstores, to sell the 
Starion line.  Digital's Starion models start as low as $1999, 
including monitor.      

     The Starion line is targeted at a segment of the small office/
home office (SOHO) retail market that Digital dubbed the tiny 
office/home office (TOHO) market -- organizations and home-based 
businesses with five or fewer employees, primarily in 
service-oriented businesses -- a market virtually ignored by other 
PC vendors.

     Today's announcement follows Digital's successful entry into 
the retail market last November.  At that time, Digital offered 
Starion models exclusively through Sam's Club and CompUSA, where 
they have been extremely well received.  

     "We are very pleased with our initial foray into the retail PC 
market," said Raymond Weadock, vice president and general manager, 
Americas, for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  "Further 
expansion into superstores makes our popular Starion PCs available 
to more small business owners where they shop."

     In addition to Pentium processing power, most Starion models 
come with a 1GB hard drive, giving users plenty of room for their 
favorite applications today and in the future.  A quad-speed CD-ROM 
drive comes standard on all but the entry-level model, so users can 
run a myriad of multimedia software, as well as music CDs.  
Quad-speed CD-ROM drives improve the performance of today's popular 
CD-ROM titles and provide the speed for the next generation of 
applications.  All minitower models include a full duplex 
speakerphone for hands-free telephone conversations.  

     Starion products are loaded with standard features, such as 8MB 
RAM, 1MB video DRAM, 14.4 data/fax modem, built-in telephone 
answering machine, and 16-bit stereo sound.  The fax feature allows 
users to send and receive faxes directly from their PC and offers 
quick connection to online services.  With the telephone answering 
machine, Starion systems act as a message center with up to 999 
private voice mailboxes.  

     A number of robust business applications are bundled with the 
Starion line, including multimedia demos and tutorials, to help 
users get right down to business, right out of the box.  
They include Intel ProShare, ClarisWorks, Lotus ScreenCam, and 
CompuServe.  In addition, MS-DOS, Microsoft Windows for Workgroups, 
and "The Complete Idiot's Guide to Windows" are pre-loaded.  The 
Starion line also supports the industry standard for Plug and Play 
and is Microsoft Windows 95 ready.

     "Our focus group research tells us that people view our Starion 
line as a sport-utility PC in a world of econoboxes," said Rod 
Keller, director, U.S. Consumer Market Development for Digital's PC 
Business Unit.  "They are rugged -- loaded with standard equipment 
-- built with a fuel-injected engine -- designed with tons of cargo 
space -- and come with a 3 year/36,000 mile limited warranty."

     The Starion 200i, Starion 400i, Starion 600i and Starion 800i 
PCs are offered exclusively through Sam's Club.  The Starion 300i, 
Starion 500i, Starion 700i and the Starion 900i PCs are offered 
through CompUSA, Incredible Universe and Nobody Beats the Wiz.  
Starion models range in price from $1999, including a 14" monitor, 
for the Starion 200i PC to $2999 for the Starion 800i PC.  The new 
Starion models carry a limited three-year warranty, with the first 
year onsite.  Included with the systems is an upgrade coupon for 
Digital's Service-in-a-Box program.  Priced at $144, the program 
provides one year of telephone support for more than 400 business 
software programs.  Digital also offers remote support via modem for 
quick problem resolution.

