            SYBASE ACHIEVES ITS HIGHEST TPC PERFORMANCE 
                     ON DIGITAL'S ALPHA SERVER 

          
         ... Award-winning AlphaServer 2100 Achieves Fastest
          Midrange TPC-C Marks Using Sybase SQL Server ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 15, 1995 --  Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Sybase, Inc., today announced the fastest TPC-C performance ever 
achieved for SYBASE SQL Server System 10. The unprecedented results 
were attained using Digital's award-winning AlphaServer 2100 system.  

     Based on independently audited tests defined by the Transaction 
Processing Performance Council (TPC), the benchmark results 
demonstrate Digital and Sybase's successful partnership to engineer 
outstanding high-performance solutions for customers. Sybase SQL 
Server 10 achieved a transaction rate of 1,708.12 transactions per 
minute (tpm-C) on the Digital AlphaServer 2100 system and price/
performance of $555/tpm-C as measured by the TPC-C V3.0 benchmark. 
The new performance benchmark was achieved using a four-processor 
AlphaServer 2100 4/275 system, Digital UNIX V3.2 operating system, 
Sybase's SQL Server 10 and the Tuxedo system, Novell's UNIX 
transaction processing monitor. 

     "The ability to deliver both excellent price/performance as 
well as industry-leading, open systems performance is a direct 
reflection of the SYBASE SQL Server capabilities," said David Sohm, 
Sybase vice president of channels and partner marketing. 
"This benchmark demonstrates the combined strength of Digital's 
Alpha architecture and SYBASE technology in meeting customers' 
large-scale data requirements. The TPC-C test suite is designed to 
simulate real-world on-line transactions."

     "Digital's servers offer customers real business value through 
powerful and scalable solutions for mission-critical applications," 
said Pauline Nist, vice president of Digital's Alpha Server Business 
Segment. "Digital and Sybase will continue to jointly engineer 
solutions with outstanding performance and price/performance." 

Digital AlphaServer 2100 System

     Digital's AlphaServer 2100 system running Sybase SQL Server 
today provides the industry's fastest published TPC-C performance 
for servers with entry prices of less than $100,000. In addition, 
customers can expect Digital to protect their current systems 
investments through future upgrades. Digital plans soon to provide 
significant performance gains for the AlphaServer 2100 systems 
through simple, cost-effective, in-cabinet upgrades featuring 
enhanced versions of Digital's 64-bit Alpha microprocessor.

     The AlphaServer 2100 family of servers is the industry's 
first RISC-based, departmental server system that combines high-
performance symmetric multiprocessing (SMP) with industry-standard 
PCI technology.  CPU expandability enables the server to handle a 
range of functions, from use as a large-capacity database server to 
a commercial application server.

     The Digital UNIX operating system, formerly known as DEC OSF/1, 
is a functionally robust, scalable, and reliable UNIX operating 
system. Digital UNIX is ideally suited to mission-critical business 
computing tasks, including data and transaction management 
solutions. 

     Datamation, a leading computer trade magazine, recently 
recognized the AlphaServer 2100 system as 1994 Server of the Year 
Award winner, based on the votes of Datamation readers and editors. 

Sybase's SQL Server

     SYBASE offers high performance, high-speed parallel backup, and 
feature enhancements to support enterprise-level client/server 
computing. 

     The SYBASE SQL Server architecture offers price/performance, 
scalability and configuration flexibility. Its architecture produces 
high OLTP performance allowing highly efficient scalability on 
Digital's servers. The SQL Server allows customers to determine the 
amount of memory and CPU resources allocated to the RDBMS in order 
to maximize the performance of both the database and other 
applications.

     Sybase, Inc. of Emeryville, California, The Enterprise Client/
Server Company, is a worldwide leader in client/server software. 
Sybase is focused in the four major client/server categories: 
databases, tools, database systems management and interoperability, 
providing desktop to enterprise scalability. The company's mission 
is to provide its customers with an open, adaptable information 
systems architecture that enables rapid business change. Sybase is 
the seventh largest independent software company in the world.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
