       GENERAL DATACOMM AND DIGITAL TEAM TO SELL ATM NETWORKS


           Leading WAN and LAN Vendors Partner to Provide
                      End-to-End ATM Solutions


MIDDLEBURY, CT -- March 20, 1995 -- General DataComm, Inc. 
(NYSE-GDC) and Digital Equipment Corporation today announced a 
comprehensive sales, marketing and technical agreement to offer 
customers integrated Asynchronous Transfer Mode (ATM) networking 
solutions. Highlighted in the agreement is a joint sales and 
marketing program to target network integrators focused on 
delivering innovative ATM solutions for federal, education, and 
financial markets. The companies have also agreed to exchange key 
technologies with a goal of accelerating the deployment of ATM 
solutions. 

     The worldwide collaboration combines GDC's strengths in wide 
area networking (WAN) with Digital's expertise in local area 
networking (LAN) to offer complete end-to-end ATM solutions. By 
combining their expertise, the companies will help ease customers' 
migration to ATM technology and facilitate deployment of such 
leading edge solutions as telemedicine and distance learning. 

     In addition to providing access to new technology, the joint 
solutions make it easy to build on customers' investments in 
existing networks. For example, customers will be able to integrate 
existing LANs into the ATM WAN environment and integrate desktop data 
with voice and video services into the enterprise ATM backbone. 
Working together, the companies will provide high-bandwidth networking 
for a campus, from campus to campus, and from a campus to a remote 
location. Multiple WAN services (Frame Relay, T1/E1, T3/E3, ATM) will 
also be integrated efficiently across an ATM WAN. 

TECHNOLOGY EXCHANGE WILL ACCELERATE DEPLOYMENT OF ATM SOLUTIONS

     The companies will share technology in a number of key areas to 
help speed deployment of production ATM solutions. Specifically, 
they will work together on technologies such as the GDC developed 
ATM Frame UNI (User Network Interface) and Digital developed FDDI 
(Fiber Distributed Data Interface). GDC and Digital will jointly 
study the interaction of LAN-based congestion management with 
ABR-based (Available Bit Rate) wide area congestion management. To 
this end, Digital will also grant a royalty free license to GDC for 
its congestion avoidance patent and flow-control technology.

     In addition, the agreement provides for extensive 
interoperability testing to ensure the total ATM solutions provide 
excellent performance and reliability. Specific areas of testing 
include network to network interface, switched virtual circuits, and 
network management. 

     "We believe this partnership holds tremendous benefits to our 
customers," said Michael C. Thurk, senior vice president of marketing
for GDC. "By combining our expertise, General DataComm and Digital
will provide end-users easy connectivity across an entire organization 
through our leading edge technology implementations. Specifically, our
combined strength will help ensure even higher performance and 
stability with data traffic." 

     "Early implementers of ATM technology tell us they want ATM 
network products that interoperate today -- they can't wait for 
standards to mature fully," said William Maro, vice president of 
product marketing and engineering for Digital's Network Product 
Business. "The close collaboration between Digital and General 
DataComm meets this need by providing customers with truly 
world-class ATM solutions." 

SOLUTIONS FEATURE GDC APEX ATM SWITCH AND DIGITAL'S NETWORK PRODUCTS

     The collaboration leverages the unique strengths of GDC's APEX 
ATM switches and Digital's DEChub family, GIGAswitch/ATM switching 
system and ATMworks family of network interface adapters to provide 
complete customer solutions. GDC's APEX ATM switch supports data, 
voice and video traffic and provides easy access to a private or 
public wide area ATM network. GDC APEX is a fully scalable system 
that can easily -- and cost effectively -- be upgraded to 
accommodate incremental network growth. The GDC ATM product family 
has an open network management system that provides carriers and 
commercial users with a highly reliable network. Along with 
Digital's GIGAswitch/ATM switch, the GDC APEX ATM switch is one of 
the few switches available to support switched virtual circuits 
(SVCs), based on the ATM Forum UNI version 3.0 (Q2931). 

     Digital's ATM products have implemented LAN ATM standards such 
as UNI 3.0, Q.2931, ILMI, IISP, and Classical IP (RFC1577). Digital 
will continue to add value to these standards and implement new 
standards as they emerge from the ATM Forum. Ideally suited for use 
in LAN backbones and high-performance workgroups, Digital's 
GIGAswitch/ATM switching system provides outstanding network 
stability by being the only switch in the industry to offer 
FLOWmaster flow control. FLOWmaster technology, in conjunction with 
Digital's low latency switch design, maximizes network performance 
and stability for bursty data traffic. The ATMworks family is 
specifically designed to increase host performance.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 

     General DataComm is the leader in providing real business 
solutions for enterprise and telecommunications networks based on 
ATM products and services. Its extensive product line includes the 
APEX family of ATM switches, LAN internetworking products, 
multiplexers, digital data sets and high-speed dial-up modems. 
Based in Middlebury, Connecticut, GDC provides communications 
solutions worldwide.
