           DIGITAL DROPS PRICES IN U.S. ON SELECTED 486 AND 
	       PENTIUM-BASED DESKTOP PERSONAL COMPUTERS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 21, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced price reductions in the United States on 20 models 
in its most popular Digital Venturis and Digital Celebris desktop PC 
lines.  The reductions of up to 20 percent produce a savings as high 
as $419 U.S. on several Venturis 486-based PCs.  The price cuts are 
effective immediately.

     A Venturis 4100/DX4/100MHz microprocessor/8MB RAM/540MB hard 
drive carries a list price of $1,880. A Pentium PC for an advanced 
user, Celebris 590 Pentium/90MHz microprocessor/8MB RAM/540 hard 
drive, is available for $2,599.

     The Venturis and Celebris personal computers introduced last 
fall feature easy access, easy-to-use capabilities such as the 
"Getting Started" menu, Plug and Play for automatic configuration of 
add-in cards, and enclosures that can be opened without tools. The 
Venturis models are designed for mainstream office use; Celebris 
models are configured for high performance applications such as 
scientific, engineering, analysis, software development, and desktop 
publishing.       

     "Our growth in desktop shipments has generated cost savings 
that we can now pass along to our reseller partners and business 
customers," explained Skip Gladfelter, vice president of America's 
marketing, Digital Personal Computer Business Unit.  Earlier last 
week, Digital PC announced price reductions of up to 19 percent for 
its Digital HiNote color notebooks.  Gladfelter said: "Both the 
notebook and desktop announcements emphasize our determination to 
remain aggressively priced with the functionality, quality, and 
support that our customers demand."

     Venturis, Celebris, and HiNote systems are available from 
resellers, distributors, systems integrators, and direct from 
Digital.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
