             DIGITAL SELECTS PARCPLACE'S VISUALWORKS AS
                CORNERSTONE OF ITS SMALLTALK STRATEGY


   ...Digital's commitment to VisualWorks demonstrates ParcPlace's
    increased visibility as a leader in providing Object-Oriented
                      Client/'Server tools ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 22, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and ParcPlace Systems, Inc., today announced a strategic partnership 
that will result in ParcPlace's VisualWorks for Digital UNIX, and 
Windows NT for Alpha being sold and supported directly by ParcPlace.  

     In December of 1993 Digital signed a licensing agreement to 
port VisualWorks to its Alpha systems. As a result of this new 
strategic partnership, ParcPlace will take over the support of 
VisualWorks to provide Digital's customers with access to 
VisualWorks, ParcPlace's powerful client and server tool for 
building portable applications using object-oriented technology. In 
addition, the partnership calls for engineering exchanges between 
the two companies, as well as cooperative sales and marketing of the 
VisualWorks product set on Digital's Alpha systems.

     Digital's strategy calls for providing its customers with a 
complete and robust Smalltalk-based development environment. 
VisualWorks, based on the ParcPlace Smalltalk programming language, 
will become the cornerstone technology in Digital's strategy to 
deliver the full features and benefits of object-oriented Smalltalk 
programming to customers as a means to address their client/server 
needs. 

     Smalltalk is playing an increasingly crucial role in the 
object-oriented development area. Market demand for Smalltalk-based 
solutions leads a rapidly growing trend to utilize object-oriented 
programming for creating new client/server applications. According 
to market research firm International Data Corp. (IDC), Smalltalk is 
the fastest growing object-oriented programming language in 
commercial MIS markets. In 1993, Smalltalk growth in this area 
exceeded 70 percent.  

     "We are excited to have this closer relationship with 
ParcPlace," stated Robert Supnik, Digital's vice president of 
Architecture and Technology in the company's Computer Systems 
Division. "VisualWorks is the recognized leader in Smalltalk-based 
application development tools, and with ParcPlace now working 
closely with Digital to provide this capability on our Alpha-based 
systems, our customers will be able to take full advantage of the 
benefits that have resulted from the coupling of our leadership 
technologies." 

     "With the growth of enterprise client/server computing, 
cross-platform portability is becoming a primary requirement for 
corporate application developers, said Bill Wesemann, vice president 
of North American sales at ParcPlace. "The addition of Digital's 
Alpha-based systems to the ParcPlace lineup will provide our 
customers access to the significant performance advantages that can 
be realized by running VisualWorks on Alpha based workstations and 
utilizing Digital UNIX or Windows NT."

     "The ParcPlace relationship is tangible evidence of Digital's 
initiatives in structuring business/technology partnerships with 
leading software vendors, across multiple industry disciplines, that 
offer customers best in class open client/server solutions," added 
William Demmer, Digital's vice president of Digital's Software 
Business Group. 

     VisualWorks enables developers to develop, deploy and maintain 
applications ranging from workgroup and departmental applications to 
complex enterprise-wide,  mission-critical applications. Included in 
VisualWorks is a Database Application Creator for rapid application 
development, an advanced graphical user interface (GUI) builder, 
database access and the ParcPlace Smalltalk object-oriented 
programming language. 

     Applications developed with VisualWorks are instantly portable 
across multiple platforms (including Windows, Windows NT, OS/2, 
Macintosh and major UNIX based systems), are scalable across the 
enterprise, and can have their functionality distributed between 
both clients and servers. 

     VisualWorks is designed to increase the productivity  of 
information systems organizations and lower software development 
costs by increasing the speed of application development, improving 
the quality of applications, and reducing long-term maintenance 
costs. 

     Digital's Alpha Systems are based on 64-bit architecture. 
Digital offers a full range of Alpha platforms ranging from 
workstations and PCs priced under $5,000 to large, multiprocessing, 
enterprise servers. 

     Beta testing for VisualWorks on Digital UNIX and Windows NT is 
currently projected to commence in the second quarter of calendar 
year 1995, with delivery targeted for early in the fourth quarter of 
calendar year 1995. VisualWorks is priced in the United States and 
Canada at $2,995 (U.S. dollars) for Windows NT, and $4,995 for 
Digital UNIX. For sales information call 1-800-759-7272 or (408) 
481-9090.  

     ParcPlace Systems, Inc. develops, markets and supports 
object-oriented solutions for the client/server market. The company 
also provides a comprehensive range of services, including customer 
support, training, on-site assistance and consulting. Headquartered 
in Sunnyvale, Calif., the company maintains offices across the 
United States and internationally with subsidiaries in Germany and 
the United Kingdom, and a network of distributors throughout the 
world.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
