                    DIGITAL NAMES JEFFREY BROOKS
             VICE PRESIDENT OF MARKETING COMMUNICATIONS


              ...Brooks to drive worldwide branding and
                    advertising communications...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- March 22, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the appointment of Jeffrey Brooks as vice president 
of marketing communications, reporting to Charlie Holleran, vice 
president of communications. The appointment is effective 
immediately.

     In this position, Brooks will be responsible for managing and 
enhancing Digital's branding, advertising, and marketing 
communications programs on a global level.  Building on a strong 
foundation, formed by Digital's current advertising campaign and 
branding programs, Brooks will integrate and unify Digital's overall 
marketing communications activities, driving toward a well-defined, 
strategic brand awareness effort worldwide.

     "We are extremely pleased to have someone with Jeff's 
impressive credentials in marketing, brand positioning and strategy 
joining Digital's staff," stated Holleran.  "With our branding 
effort well under way, I see Jeff becoming a major contributor in 
accelerating the company's brand communications efforts in support 
of attaining a unified corporate image in the marketplace."

     Brooks comes to Digital after spending 17 years with Sony 
Corporation of America, where he held a succession of senior 
management positions, including senior vice president of marketing 
communications and advertising.  In this position, he was 
responsible for defining and implementing marketing and brand 
strategies, corporate image, advertising and media management, 
retail merchandising and partnership affiliations for all of Sony's 
consumer and business-to-business activities.      

     Brooks is a graduate of the Rochester Institute of Technology, 
where he earned his bachelor of science degree and is a graduate of 
Harvard University's Advanced Management Program.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
