               DIGITAL AND PROCESS SOFTWARE TO PROVIDE
                INDUSTRIAL-STRENGTH INTERNET SERVERS


       Digital Offering Process' Premier World Wide Web Server
              Software Package on Windows NT Platforms


MAYNARD Mass. - March 23, 1995 - Digital Equipment Corporation and 
Process Software Corporation of Framingham, Mass. today announced a 
worldwide distribution partnership making Digital a reseller of 
Purveyor, Process Software's new World Wide Web (WWW) server 
software package for Windows NT.  This agreement benefits customers 
looking for a powerful, yet cost-effective means of achieving 
business results from the Internet.  Beginning immediately, Digital
will offer Purveyor for Alpha NT and Intel NT platforms for a U.S. 
list price of $1,995.

     "Customers want to do business on the Internet in the computing 
style they prefer," said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of 
Digital's Internet Business Group.  "They are asking for an NT 
alternative to UNIX.  With this agreement, Digital and Process 
Software are providing customers with a supported Windows NT based 
solution that is affordable and easy to install and use."

     "This agreement represents tremendous news for Windows NT users 
around the world," said Philip Denzer, president, Process Software 
Corporation. "It means that Purveyor is available immediately, on a 
worldwide basis, from Digital -- one of the premier Windows NT vendors."

     Windows NT based Internet servers are particularly attractive 
because solutions are scalable and the need for higher performance 
does not increase the system management complexity or difficulty.

     Purveyor allows corporations to publish public and confidential 
multimedia information on the Internet as well as their corporate 
local area networks (LANS).  With Purveyor's sample forms and 
templates, organizations can publish information such as product and 
corporate news on the Internet all with the ease-of-use of Windows 
NT.  By using Purveyor on the LAN, companies are able to easily 
disseminate and update internal information such as employee 
handbooks and on-line training courses, further heightening 
efficiency and productivity.

     Digital and Process Software will be giving demonstrations of 
Purveyor at the NetWorld+Interop trade show in Las Vegas from March 
28-30 (Booth 3627 and 2358 respectively).

     Based on the widely-used public domain HTTP server from the 
European Microsoft Windows Academic Centre (EMWAC), commercial 
enhancements available through Process Software include advanced 
security features managed through a Microsoft Windows graphical user 
interface, as well as support for HTTP, FTP and Gopher proxy 
servers. In addition, full logging capabilities are provided by the 
server giving users the ability to log and track incoming requests.  
Associated utilities also are included for presenting and analyzing 
the traffic data captured by the server.

     This announcement is the second partnership agreement between 
the two companies in the last four months. In October 1994, Digital 
announced it had selected Process Software as its TCP/IP Technology 
Partner for OpenVMS and that elements of Process' popular TCPware 
product family would be integrated into Digital's TCP/IP Services 
for OpenVMS product.

     Digital's Internet Business Group (IBG) provides companies with 
cost-effective services and products to produce business results 
with the use of Internet technologies. To do this, Digital's IBG is 
sharing its knowledge and expertise with organizations who want to 
develop new business structures, improve productivity and lower 
costs associated with conducting business on the Internet.  

     Established in 1984, Process Software Corporation designs, 
develops, and markets TCP/IP and Internet software solutions 
worldwide, and backs all of them with one of the most comprehensive 
service and support programs in the industry. Process Software's 
complete line of TCP/IP product and service offerings include 
solutions for the Windows NT, Windows, and OpenVMS platforms.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations 
complete and win in today's global marketplace.  
